meta {
  name: Subscription - Checkout
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/subscription/checkout
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "plan_id": {{planId}},
    "interval": "monthly"
  }
}

docs {
  Starts a Stripe Checkout session for the given plan and billing interval:
  `monthly`, `quarterly`, `yearly`, or `lifetime`. Requires the
  `billing.manage` permission.

  The three recurring intervals open (or swap) a Stripe subscription:

  - No subscription yet: returns `data.checkout_url` to redirect the user
    to Stripe Checkout (trial days are applied if the plan has any).
  - Existing subscription: swaps its price in place and returns the updated
    `data.subscription` instead of a checkout URL.

  `lifetime` is a one-time purchase instead — a `mode=payment` Checkout
  Session with no subscription behind it. It returns `data.checkout_url`
  alongside the `data.plan_grant` recorded for it, which stays `pending`
  until Stripe confirms payment via `checkout.session.completed`. Read the
  resulting entitlement from `GET /billing`'s `current_plan`, since no
  subscription exists to read a plan off.

  - Returns `422` if the plan has no Stripe price for that interval — check
    a plan's `available_intervals` before offering one.
  - Returns `422` on a lifetime purchase of a plan the workspace already
    holds an active grant for.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data }`.
}
